        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-5": {
      "id": "authored-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision: transport and client installation remain in the MCP package. The shared filesystem server and pure library do not depend on MCP or Agent Kernel. Runtime state belongs to an authenticated local daemon; source documents remain on disk."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-6": {
      "id": "authored-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why: clients share one endpoint while Kernel hosts can save through the filesystem library independently. Applies to future client adapters and transports."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-7": {
      "id": "authored-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
